<h2>What TMJ disorders actually are</h2>
<p>"TMJ" refers to your temporomandibular joints — the two joints that connect your lower jaw to your skull. TMJ disorders cover a range of problems: muscle tension, joint inflammation, disc displacement, and pain triggered by grinding or clenching. Symptoms include jaw pain, clicking or popping, headaches, ear fullness, and limited jaw movement.</p>

<h2>How we evaluate</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Clinical exam of the muscles and joints</li>
  <li>Bite analysis and review of tooth wear patterns</li>
  <li>Imaging if needed</li>
  <li>Conversation about stress, sleep, and any jaw habits</li>
</ul>

<h2>Custom night guards</h2>
<p>A custom night guard is a thin, hard acrylic appliance molded precisely to your teeth. It protects your enamel from grinding, takes pressure off the joints, and often reduces morning soreness and headaches significantly. We make them in two visits — impression, then delivery and fit-check.</p>

<h2>Beyond the night guard</h2>
<p>For more complex TMJ cases we may recommend a daytime appliance, physical therapy referrals, or a coordinated plan with an outside TMJ-focused provider. We'll tell you honestly what's likely to help and what isn't.</p>
